{"id": "en_story_blockbuster", "tag": "BUSINESS FAILS", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#4C8DFF", "lang": "en", "total": 77.53, "segments": [{"text": "2 founders walk into a giant corporate boardroom with an offer that changes history forever.", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.38}, {"text": "In 2000, Netflix founders Reed Hastings and Marc Randolph offer to sell Netflix to Blockbuster.", "start": 4.86, "end": 9.6}, {"text": "They ask Blockbuster for 50 million dollars to buy Netflix, but Blockbuster quickly declines it.", "start": 10.18, "end": 14.76}, {"text": "Netflix CFO Barry McCarthy says that they are actually laughed right out of the room.", "start": 14.865, "end": 18.82}, {"text": "At the time, Blockbuster dominates and relies heavily on its profitable and costly late fees.", "start": 19.38, "end": 24.02}, {"text": "The massive rental giant peaks around 2004 with about 9,000 physical retail stores open everywhere.", "start": 24.56, "end": 29.56}, {"text": "Those 9,000 stores seem unbeatable, but the fortune of the giant company slowly starts falling.", "start": 30.0, "end": 34.72}, {"text": "The reliance on late fees cannot save the business as conditions change over the decade.", "start": 35.02, "end": 38.5}, {"text": "The massive empire collapses, and Blockbuster files for bankruptcy in September 2010 after huge losses.", "start": 39.1, "end": 44.38}, {"text": "Meanwhile, the small startup that got rejected continues to grow into a global entertainment giant.", "start": 45.08, "end": 49.6}, {"text": "Netflix grows relentlessly and eventually becomes worth hundreds of billions of dollars across the globe.", "start": 50.16, "end": 54.54}, {"text": "Today, exactly 1 single privately owned Blockbuster store remains standing open out in Bend, Oregon.", "start": 54.54, "end": 60.54}, {"text": "That lonely store in Bend, Oregon is all that remains of the former 9,000 stores.", "start": 61.02, "end": 64.72}, {"text": "The leaders who laughed back in 2000 watched their entire kingdom completely vanish into history.", "start": 65.24, "end": 69.6}, {"text": "Did Blockbuster make the biggest business mistake ever by rejecting that 50 million dollar deal?", "start": 70.2, "end": 74.38}], "words": [["2", 0.0, 0.104], ["founders", 0.32, 0.62], ["walk", 0.62, 0.86], ["into", 0.86, 1.06], ["a", 1.06, 1.16], ["giant", 1.16, 1.52], ["corporate", 1.52, 2.0], ["boardroom", 2.0, 2.5], ["with", 2.5, 2.72], ["an", 2.72, 2.84], ["offer", 2.84, 3.0], ["that", 3.0, 3.22], ["changes", 3.22, 3.48], ["history", 3.48, 3.98], ["forever.", 3.98, 4.38], ["In", 4.86, 5.06], ["2000,", 5.06, 5.5], ["Netflix", 5.92, 6.0], ["founders", 6.0, 6.48], ["Reed", 6.48, 6.8], ["Hastings", 6.8, 7.18], ["and", 7.18, 7.38], ["Marc", 7.1899999999999995, 7.379], ["Randolph", 7.56, 7.92], ["offer", 7.92, 8.2], ["to", 8.2, 8.34], ["sell", 8.34, 8.56], ["Netflix", 8.56, 8.8], ["to", 8.8, 9.18], ["Blockbuster.", 9.18, 9.6], ["They", 10.18, 10.42], ["ask", 10.42, 10.62], ["Blockbuster", 10.62, 11.0], ["for", 11.0, 11.26], ["50", 11.26, 11.58], ["million", 11.58, 11.9], ["dollars", 11.694, 12.11], ["to", 11.9, 12.38], ["buy", 12.38, 12.52], ["Netflix,", 12.52, 12.8], ["but", 13.14, 13.28], ["Blockbuster", 13.28, 13.76], ["quickly", 13.76, 14.2], ["declines", 14.2, 14.62], ["it.", 14.62, 14.76], ["Netflix", 14.865, 15.28], ["CFO", 15.66, 15.86], ["Barry", 15.86, 16.12], ["McCarthy", 16.12, 16.38], ["says", 16.38, 16.7], ["that", 16.7, 16.84], ["they", 16.84, 16.96], ["are", 16.96, 17.04], ["actually", 17.04, 17.32], ["laughed", 17.32, 17.64], ["right", 17.64, 18.12], ["out", 18.12, 18.4], ["of", 18.4, 18.5], ["the", 18.5, 18.58], ["room.", 18.58, 18.82], ["At", 19.38, 19.66], ["the", 19.66, 19.74], ["time,", 19.74, 19.94], ["Blockbuster", 20.32, 20.68], ["dominates", 20.68, 21.3], ["and", 21.3, 21.44], ["relies", 21.44, 21.6], ["heavily", 21.6, 21.98], ["on", 21.98, 22.18], ["its", 22.18, 22.28], ["profitable",